	(text "All parts chosen for JLCPCB / NextPCB Rev0 assembly; see\nresearch/*.md for availability and pricing (checked 2026-09-01)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 195 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5bad2468-5c5f-44af-bb2c-1f9970aa3e3c")
	)
	(text "RPi Camera LED interposer: sits between a Raspberry Pi and its camera.\nMIPI lanes, I2C, GND and 3V3 pass straight through J1 -> J2.\nU1 (I2C slave on the camera bus) drives the camera GPIO pins 11/12,\nPWM-drives the illumination LEDs and reads ambient light on its ADC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6313a208-6745-45c8-b92e-ff7d2195625c")
	)
	(text "R6/R7 (0R, DNP) are a bypass: fit them to wire the Pi's CAM_IO pins\nstraight to the camera, e.g. when U1 is unpopulated. Left off, U1 sits in\nthe middle -- it watches the Pi on PD5/PD6 and drives the camera on PA1/PA2.\nDo not fit them while U1 drives: 0R gives contention no current limit."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.256 120.65 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "858e767f-5f93-49c1-be12-275382b575b8")
	)
	(text "LED current is set by R3/R4 against the 3V3 rail (about 30-40mA each\nwith Vf=2.9V). Total draw comes from the Pi camera 3V3 supply - keep\nthe duty/current within the Pi's camera connector budget."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 183 32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9b2cadfa-bc85-44f7-84ef-92d4a59d891b")
	)
	(text "SOP-16 bonds no two ports to one pin, so PD1/SWIO is programming only\nand PC3/T1CH3 drives the LED gate: no LED flicker while flashing firmware.\nPC6, PC7, PD4 and PC0 are spare. PD7 is left unused on purpose: it is NRST\nuntil the RST_MODE option byte says otherwise, so a Pi GPIO on it would\nreset the MCU on a factory-fresh part."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 95 193 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "eea18d7f-1257-4d78-8e7b-924bcbbd6678")
	)
